This gem is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It links nothing
and vendors nothing: the library and its typelib come from the system at run
time, so a recipient remains free to replace them with their own build. Nothing
in this repository is derived from libspelling's source -- a typelib is a
machine-readable description of an interface, and what this gem does with it is
read it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
enchant, and the dictionaries
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

libspelling-1 does no spelling itself either. It asks enchant, which asks
whichever backend the user has installed -- usually hunspell -- and the word
lists those backends read are packaged separately again, under their own
licences. None of that is in this repository, and which dictionaries exist on a
machine is why Spelling::Provider#list_languages has to be asked rather than
assumed.

  https://abiword.github.io/enchant/
  Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ruby-gnome
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The loader is GObjectIntrospection::Loader, from ruby-gnome, and is written on
the model of ruby-gnome's own gtksourceview5 and libsecret loaders. It appears
here as a gem dependency rather than as copied code.

